{
  "_comment": [
    "Record of the Express -> FastAPI migration, and the URL manifest the",
    "parity harnesses in tools/ read.",
    "",
    "This file no longer drives any routing. The migration is COMPLETE: nginx",
    "sends the whole API to one upstream (frontend/nginx.conf.template) and the",
    "Vite dev server does the same, so there is nothing left to generate.",
    "",
    "It is still worth keeping. tools/parity.py walks these entries to compare",
    "the two backends URL by URL, which stays useful for as long as Express is",
    "deployed as the rollback target -- and it is the inventory that proves all",
    "69 routes were accounted for.",
    "",
    "match: 'exact' -> one URL only; 'prefix' -> that path and everything under it.",
    "samples: extra URLs (with query strings) the parity check should compare.",
    "_skip_parity: not byte-comparable (rendered images, OAuth redirects)."
  ],
